We immediately notice a call to printf (line 37), which is vulnerable to a classic stack-based leak if a variable is passed directly to it instead of being printed with a format specifier such as %s, %d, %x, etc.

After the call to gets, the program performs a comparison (cmp) between eax, which has been loaded with the value of the address 0x804988c, and 0x40, which corresponds to the decimal value 64.

```bash
